    "atdd_status_md": "## Adversarial TDD Status\nFeature: striped-block-cache\nMode: greenfield\nMax rounds: 3\nCurrent round: 3\nStatus: complete\nSubstage: verified\n\n## Round History\n| Round | Analyst vectors | Breaker tests | Confirmed bugs | Theoretical | Status |\n|-------|----------------|---------------|----------------|-------------|--------|\n| 1 | 16 | 53 | 2 (sentinel collision, test threshold) | 1 (M2 close exception) | complete |\n| 2 | 6 | 7 | 2 (thundering herd, stale re-insertion) | 3 (double close, post-close ops, capacity lie) | complete |\n| 3 | 4 | 3 | 2 (eviction false positive, unbounded join) | 1 (exception type propagation) | complete |\n",
    "known_issues_md": "# Known Issues \u2014 striped-block-cache\n<!-- Maintained by Spec Analyst. Do not edit manually. -->\n\n## Resolved patterns\n<!-- RESOLVED: confirmed bugs \u2014 Breaker test failed, Implementer fixed -->\n\n### RESOLVED R1-1: Hash distribution test threshold (Round 1)\nThe original test expected perfect distribution (`assertEquals(16, size)`) for 16 items\ninto 4 hash bins. Splitmix64 achieves max-bucket=5 for these inputs, causing 2 evictions.\nTest threshold relaxed to `assertTrue(size >= 12)`. This is a test calibration issue, not\nan implementation bug \u2014 the hash function distributes correctly per ADR.\n\n### RESOLVED R2-1: getOrLoad thundering herd (Round 2)\nThe inherited default `getOrLoad` from `BlockCache` performs `get()` then `put()` as two\nseparate locked operations. Under concurrent access with the same key, ALL threads see a\ncache miss and ALL invoke the loader independently. Fixed by overriding `getOrLoad` in\n`StripedBlockCache` with per-key load deduplication via `ConcurrentHashMap<LoadKey,\nCompletableFuture<MemorySegment>>`.\n**Test:** `getOrLoadThunderingHerdMultipleThreads`\n\n### RESOLVED R2-2: Evict-during-getOrLoad stale re-insertion (Round 2)\nA concurrent `getOrLoad` that sees a cache miss before `evict()` completes will call\n`put()` after eviction, re-inserting a block for an sstableId that was just evicted. This\ncauses the cache to serve stale data for a compacted SSTable. Fixed by adding an eviction\nversion counter: `evict()` bumps the version, `getOrLoad` captures it before loading and\nskips `put()` if the version changed.\n**Test:** `evictDuringGetOrLoadDoesNotReinsertStaleBlock`\n\n### RESOLVED R3-1: Eviction version false positive \u2014 global counter too coarse (Round 3)\nThe round 2 fix used a global `AtomicLong evictionVersion`. An `evict(sstableId=X)` during\na `getOrLoad(sstableId=Y)` caused the valid load for Y to skip caching, even though Y was\nNOT evicted. Fixed by replacing global version with per-sstableId versions via\n`ConcurrentHashMap<Long, AtomicLong>`.\n**Test:** `evictOfDifferentSstableIdDoesNotPreventCachingCurrentLoad`\n\n### RESOLVED R3-2: Unbounded blocking in getOrLoad waiter (Round 3)\nWaiting threads used `CompletableFuture.join()` which has no timeout. A hung loader blocked\nall waiting threads indefinitely, violating bounded-blocking guidelines. Fixed by using\n`future.get(1, SECONDS)` \u2014 on timeout, the waiting thread falls through to load\nindependently via the loader (degrades to double-load rather than deadlock).\n**Test:** `getOrLoadWaiterDoesNotBlockIndefinitelyOnSlowLoader`\n\n## Tendencies\n<!-- TENDENCY: recurring implementation anti-patterns the Implementer defaults to -->\n\n### TENDENCY T1-1: Sentinel value collision in builder (Round 1)\nBuilder used `-1` as sentinel for \"shardCount not set\", but user calling `.shardCount(-1)`\nwas indistinguishable from \"not set\". Fixed by adding a `shardCountSet` boolean flag.\n**Watch for:** any builder that uses a user-settable value as a sentinel.\n\n### TENDENCY T2-1: Inheriting default interface methods without concurrency audit (Round 2)\nThe default `getOrLoad` on `BlockCache` is correct for single-threaded use but has TOCTOU\nand stale-insertion races under concurrency. `StripedBlockCache` initially inherited it\nwithout analysis. **Watch for:** any default method on an interface that a thread-safe\nimplementation inherits \u2014 audit for atomicity before accepting the default.\n\n### TENDENCY T3-1: Overly coarse-grained invalidation (Round 3)\nRound 2 fix used a global eviction counter, causing unrelated evictions to invalidate valid\nconcurrent loads. Round 3 refined to per-sstableId granularity. **Watch for:** global counters\nor flags used to coordinate between independent logical entities \u2014 scope the coordination\nto the specific entity.\n\n## Protected by ADR\n<!-- ADR-PROTECTED: risks accepted by an architecture decision. Cite the ADR slug. -->\n\n### ADR-PROTECTED: Non-atomic cross-stripe eviction\nADR `cross-stripe-eviction` \u00a7What-This-Decision-Does-NOT-Solve explicitly accepts that\neviction is not atomic across stripes. A concurrent `get()` might briefly see an entry in\nan un-evicted stripe during the sweep.\n\n### ADR-PROTECTED: Imperfect hash distribution\nADR `stripe-hash-function` \u00a7What-This-Decision-Does-NOT-Solve explicitly states \"Does not\nguarantee perfectly uniform distribution (slight skew is acceptable).\"\n\n## Language/runtime impossible\n<!-- IMPOSSIBLE: vectors that cannot occur in this language/runtime. State why. -->\n\n### IMPOSSIBLE: Manual memory corruption of shard array\nJava arrays are bounds-checked at runtime. `ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException` is thrown on\ninvalid index \u2014 cannot silently corrupt memory. The `& 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFL` in the hash\nensures non-negative values, and `& (shardCount - 1)` ensures the index is within bounds.\n",
    "gaps_md": ""
  }
